					<description><![CDATA[<p>This content is copyright to <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.artemis.bm</a> and should not appear anywhere else, or an infringement has occurred.</p>
<p>Specialist insurance-linked securities (ILS) investment manager Leadenhall Capital Partners LLP is monitoring investor appetite for different ILS products, while leveraging artificial intelligence to increase productivity and improve its risk analysis, CEO Luca Albertini told Artemis. Launched in 2008, Leadenhall Capital Partners has built a proven track-record across the ILS market, with strategies focused on reinsurance [&#8230;]</p>
<p><a href="https://www.artemis.bm/news/leadenhall-positions-for-growth-via-ils-product-discipline-and-controlled-ai-use-albertini/">Leadenhall positions for growth via ILS product discipline and controlled AI use: Albertini</a> was published by: <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.Artemis.bm</a><br />
Our <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/deal-directory/">catastrophe bond deal directory</a><br />
Sign up for <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/e-newsletter/">our free weekly email newsletter here</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>This content is copyright to <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.artemis.bm</a> and should not appear anywhere else, or an infringement has occurred.</p>
<p>Specialist insurance-linked securities (ILS) investment manager Leadenhall Capital Partners LLP is monitoring investor appetite for different ILS products, while leveraging artificial intelligence to increase productivity and improve its risk analysis, CEO Luca Albertini told Artemis.<br />
<span id="more-149104"></span><br />
<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-attachment-id="134148" data-permalink="https://www.artemis.bm/news/preserving-ils-balance-between-cedent-support-investor-reward-essential-albertini-leadenhall/attachment/luca-albertini-leadenhall-capital-partners-2/" data-orig-file="https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/luca-albertini-leadenhall-capital-partners.jpg" data-orig-size="700,438" data-comments-opened="0" data-image-title="luca-albertini-leadenhall-capital-partners" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/luca-albertini-leadenhall-capital-partners.jpg" class="alignright wp-image-134148" src="https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/luca-albertini-leadenhall-capital-partners.jpg" alt="luca-albertini-leadenhall-capital-partners" width="370" height="232" srcset="https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/luca-albertini-leadenhall-capital-partners.jpg 700w, https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/luca-albertini-leadenhall-capital-partners-300x188.jpg 300w, https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/luca-albertini-leadenhall-capital-partners-200x125.jpg 200w, https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/luca-albertini-leadenhall-capital-partners-350x219.jpg 350w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 370px) 100vw, 370px" />Launched in 2008, Leadenhall Capital Partners has built a proven track-record across the ILS market, with strategies focused on reinsurance opportunities, catastrophe bonds, life and alternative credit insurance linked investments.</p>
<p>During a recent interview with Artemis around the key conference season, Luca Albertini, CEO and one of the founders of the firm, discussed how he hopes to differentiate Leadenhall to attract clients through the rest of 2026 and into 2027.</p>
<p>“We hope investors will see in Leadenhall an established player (we launched in 2008) with access to a deep pool of experience underwriting skills, with a stable senior management team and the support of a large multinational financial services group (MSI), whilst maintaining independence in the investment decisions and a corporate structure (partnership) which strongly aligns the investment team with the interest of our investors,” Albertini told Artemis.</p>
<p>Expanding further on this, the CEO then detailed what opportunities he currently sees within the market that Leadenhall can use to grow its business further into 2027 and beyond.</p>
<p>“Leadenhall has seen a significant growth in its AUM in 2026, whilst remaining focused on its core offering,” Albertini said.</p>
<p>He continued: “The team has capacity to further grow its current offering, but we constantly monitor investor appetite for different products and we assess the opportunity in line with our view of the medium term potential for those opportunities and our own skills set needed to underwrite the underlying products.”</p>
<p>Addressing the firm’s technology roadmap, Albertini highlighted how Leadenhall is adopting a measured approach to artificial intelligence, balancing enterprise-wide adoption with strict oversight.</p>
<p>“Leadenhall has invested in AI, and is currently having business access to one leading platform . Each team and each function in the firm is challenged to think how to use AI to increase productivity and improve our ability to analyse risk,” the Leadenhall Capital Partners CEO said.</p>
<p>Concluding: “We are doing this however in a controlled way and lots of attention is also put on “hallucinations” and on the quality of the output, so the validation of what AI generates remains key.”</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://www.artemis.bm/interviews/">Read all of our interviews with ILS market and reinsurance sector professionals here</a></strong>.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.artemis.bm/news/leadenhall-positions-for-growth-via-ils-product-discipline-and-controlled-ai-use-albertini/">Leadenhall positions for growth via ILS product discipline and controlled AI use: Albertini</a> was published by: <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.Artemis.bm</a><br />
Our <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/deal-directory/">catastrophe bond deal directory</a><br />
Sign up for <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/e-newsletter/">our free weekly email newsletter here</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
		<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">149104</post-id>	</item>
		<item>
		<title>Swiss Re says increased reinsurance supply a positive, will align alt capital where it makes sense</title>
		<link>https://www.artemis.bm/news/swiss-re-says-increased-reinsurance-supply-a-positive-will-align-alt-capital-where-it-makes-sense/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=swiss-re-says-increased-reinsurance-supply-a-positive-will-align-alt-capital-where-it-makes-sense</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jack Willard]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:30:13 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Reinsurance News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Alternative reinsurance capital]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[capital markets]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Insurance linked securities]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[reinsurance]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.artemis.bm/?p=150946</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>This content is copyright to <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.artemis.bm</a> and should not appear anywhere else, or an infringement has occurred.</p>
<p>Speaking ahead of the 2026 Baden-Baden gathering, Leopoldo Camara, Head of P&#38;C Reinsurance Northern, Central &#38; Eastern Europe at Swiss Re outlined that more reinsurance capital is needed in the market to address growing, interconnected risks, while also emphasising that the reinsurer will use its deep risk expertise to align alternative capital where it makes sense. [&#8230;]</p>
<p><a href="https://www.artemis.bm/news/swiss-re-says-increased-reinsurance-supply-a-positive-will-align-alt-capital-where-it-makes-sense/">Swiss Re says increased reinsurance supply a positive, will align alt capital where it makes sense</a> was published by: <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.Artemis.bm</a><br />
Our <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/deal-directory/">catastrophe bond deal directory</a><br />
Sign up for <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/e-newsletter/">our free weekly email newsletter here</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>This content is copyright to <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.artemis.bm</a> and should not appear anywhere else, or an infringement has occurred.</p>
<p>Speaking ahead of the 2026 Baden-Baden gathering, Leopoldo Camara, Head of P&amp;C Reinsurance Northern, Central &amp; Eastern Europe at Swiss Re outlined that more reinsurance capital is needed in the market to address growing, interconnected risks, while also emphasising that the reinsurer will use its deep risk expertise to align alternative capital where it makes sense.<br />
<span id="more-150946"></span><br />
<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-attachment-id="132905" data-permalink="https://www.artemis.bm/news/cat-bond-market-momentum-positions-2025-for-exceptional-year-of-issuance-swiss-re/attachment/swiss-re-building-logo-2/" data-orig-file="https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/swiss-re-building-logo.jpg" data-orig-size="800,500" data-comments-opened="0" data-image-title="swiss-re-building-logo" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/swiss-re-building-logo.jpg" class="alignright wp-image-132905" src="https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/swiss-re-building-logo.jpg" alt="swiss-re-building-logo" width="370" height="231" srcset="https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/swiss-re-building-logo.jpg 800w, https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/swiss-re-building-logo-300x188.jpg 300w, https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/swiss-re-building-logo-768x480.jpg 768w, https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/swiss-re-building-logo-200x125.jpg 200w, https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/swiss-re-building-logo-350x219.jpg 350w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 370px) 100vw, 370px" />“We see more capital flowing into the markets and into the reinsurance industry, and we think that is actually good news because more capital is needed to address the growing risks that we all need to deal with,” Camara explained.</p>
<p>Moreover, Camara underscored that different types of capital play different roles across the industry, highlighting the company’s long-standing commitment to reinsurance and its combination of capital with deep risk expertise.</p>
<p>“Our capital, the Swiss Re capital, is committed to the industry for a very long time. It is here to do multi-line reinsurance. So, we do life and health and P&amp;C, we do short tail and long tail,” the executive said.</p>
<p>“The core business proposition of our capital, the core mandate is on the right side of the balance sheet. So, we&#8217;re here to play to pay claims. That&#8217;s our main promise: paying claims,” Camara continued.</p>
<p>“And we issue this promise, bringing alongside capital, deep risk expertise that we have acquired over more than 100 years. And this deep risk expertise, in our view, is absolutely indispensable to arrange risk transfer in a sustainable way, to help mitigate the risk, to actually measure and quantify the risk, to develop new risk transfer approaches, and also to align alternative capital when this makes sense.</p>
<p>“So, this is our kind of capital. That&#8217;s the kind of capital we&#8217;re bringing to Baden-Baden, and we actually see that our capital is in high demand.”</p>
<p>On the demand side, Camara noted that Swiss Re was seeing increasing amounts of systemic risk, with exposures becoming more interconnected and therefore more systemic.</p>
<p>The executive identified four key factors driving this trend: larger individual risks, intensified geographic clustering, enhanced integration of supply chain networks, and growing digital and social networks that amplify risk propagation.</p>
<p>“Larger individual risks, the prime example that comes to mind are data centers, where we see insured value concentrations in excess of billions, sometimes even tens of billions, in very small, limited locations. So, increasing amounts of large risk concentration,” Camara added.</p>
<p>Going back to alternative capital, Camara highlighted during the Q&amp;A portion of the briefing, that Swiss Re has a long-standing track record in the space, through the use of its third-party capital markets focused Alternative Capital Partners (ACP) division.</p>
<p>“Swiss Re has a long-standing track record in a unit called Alternative Capital Partners. So we&#8217;re quite used and experienced in also deploying that kind of capital or supporting that kind of capital with what we bring to the table to enable alternative capital to actually take on risk,” the executive said.</p>
<p>At the 2026 Monte Carlo Rendez-Vous de Septembre (RVS) reinsurance industry event, Urs Baertschi, Chief Executive Officer, of P&amp;C Reinsurance, underscored the importance of the reinsurers Alternative Capital Partners division, <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/news/swiss-re-expects-to-continue-being-a-meaningful-participant-in-alternative-capital-baertschi/">whilst also stating that Swiss Re expects to continue to be a “meaningful participant in that market.”</a></p>
<p><a href="https://www.artemis.bm/news/swiss-re-says-increased-reinsurance-supply-a-positive-will-align-alt-capital-where-it-makes-sense/">Swiss Re says increased reinsurance supply a positive, will align alt capital where it makes sense</a> was published by: <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.Artemis.bm</a><br />
Our <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/deal-directory/">catastrophe bond deal directory</a><br />
Sign up for <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/e-newsletter/">our free weekly email newsletter here</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
